      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hungry Horse is located in central Flathead County at the confluence of the Flathead River and its South Fork.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hungry_Horse%2C_Montana",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Hungry Horse grew from a wartime boom when the U.S. Bureau of Reclamation built the dam and installed over a hundred prefabricated buildings for workers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hungry_Horse%2C_Montana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hungry Horse Dam, finished in 1953, stands 564 feet tall—Montana's highest—and ranks as the eleventh largest concrete dam in the United States.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitmt.com/places-to-go/cities-and-towns/hungry-horse.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The visitor center at Hungry Horse Dam opens guided tours that showcase the dam’s engineering and surrounding wilderness.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://visitmt.com/places-to-go/cities-and-towns/hungry-horse.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A trail to the historic fire lookout meanders through Flathead National Forest, where towering pines, wildflowers, and occasional wildlife sightings make the walk memorable.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoveringmontana.com/things-to-do-in-hungry-horse-montana/",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Hungry Horse’s name comes from a legend of two horses, Tex and Jerry, who escaped and nearly starved in deep snow along the South Fork.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
